implementationPlan.description:
postflight-vm-route.sh [strong gate]: the end-to-end rows. Add a new `( ... )` subshell section after the [strong intent] block (its `echo "[strong intent] ok G1-G7 and G8"` line) and before `echo "PASS postflight-vm-route.sh"`. Name it `[strong gate]`, as CQ-M07s step 3 and CQ-M07t step 3 expect. Every existing row and assertion stays byte-identical (DoD 3).

SETUP inside the subshell:
- SG_FAKE=$ROOT_DIR/scripts/tests/postflight-fake-check-dispatch.js, SG_WITNESS=$TMP_DIR/sg-witness, SG_READY='{"profile":"verified-local","ready":true,"missingCapabilities":[]}'.
- Export MOE_AGENT_SEAT_PATH (the fake seat), GIT_AUTHOR_NAME, GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL, GIT_COMMITTER_NAME and GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL, and all five credentials non-empty. OPENAI_API_KEY is the codex seat's VM credential, so no account fixture is needed.
- VMR_SETUP=sg_fixture. It does three things. First, vmj_fixture's git part: .gitignore and seed.txt on main, then moe/control. Second, it merges these settings with node: {autoCommit:true, checkpointPush:false, commitBoardState:false, qualityGate:"printf ran > '<SG_WITNESS>'"}. That gate is the canary: a host run writes the witness. Third, it runs rm -f on the witness, saves SG_BASE to $TMP_DIR/sg-base, and exports FAKE_CLAIM_WORKSPACE and FAKE_CTX_WORKSPACE ({mode:worktree, target:main}) and FAKE_TASK_STATUS=REVIEW, so the run is a worker completion.
- Each row: `vmr_run SG-<x> worker codex "$SG_READY" on 0 FAKE_ATTEMPT_PROFILE=<p> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH=<path> FAKE_CHECK_DISPATCH=<mode> ...`. The VM route runs run_vm_job before any codex branch, so no host CLI and no argv probe runs. The fake seat's job admits vm-job.txt and land_vm_candidate commits it to moe/task/task-postflight, so M differs from B.

CHECKER. One node checker, `sg_check ROW KIND CODE [ENV]`, reads evidence-rpcs.jsonl, FAKE_CALL_LOG, OUT (with ANSI escapes stripped: the wrapper's colours are unconditional), the attempt record, landing-retry.json and git.
- Every row: REC is absent (no host CLI), exit 0, and exactly one record_candidate (M = its treeSha, B = SG_BASE). The output never contains DISPATCH-CANARY.
- Strong rows:
  - the witness is absent, there is no record_check_run row and no `Post-flight: quality gate:` line;
  - every check-dispatch row has argv exactly ['--project', PROJECT, '--task', 'task-postflight', '--commit', X], with X 40-hex;
  - that row also records tree M, parents [B], heads refs/heads/main = B, candidateId = record_candidate's id, and credentials [];
  - after the run, `git for-each-ref --contains X` is empty (never published).
- KIND pass (SG-pass, DoD 1):
  - main = C, C differs from X, C's parents are [B] and its tree is M;
  - the check-dispatch row precedes the committed completion record_commit row and finalize_attempt;
  - finalize is landed with landedRevision C;
  - there is one `[OK] check VMs passed every owed check of candidate <id>.` line and no MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_REFUSED line.
  Pin no receipts and no journal keys: CQ-M07t adds them.
- KIND host. Rows: SG-legacy (no FAKE_ATTEMPT_PROFILE) and SG-observe (FAKE_ATTEMPT_PROFILE=observe), both with MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH=$SG_FAKE. Expect:
  - no check-dispatch row;
  - the witness present, which proves the canary is live;
  - one record_check_run with outcome passed;
  - main = C with parent B;
  - one `[OK] qualityGate passed.` line.
- KIND refused:
  - main = B;
  - exactly one completion record_commit row: ['failed','MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE', pushed false];
  - exactly one finalize_attempt {outcome:'unlanded', unlandedReason:'gate', targetTip:B, landedRevision:null};
  - landing-retry.json {reason:'gate', count:1}, whose rescueRef resolves to the tip of moe/task/task-postflight;
  - the attempt record's phase is 'closed';
  - FAKE_CALL_LOG holds no set_task_status, complete_task, release_task, report_blocked, qa_approve or qa_reject;
  - exactly one line `[WARN] MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_REFUSED: <CODE>[ environment=<ENV>]`;
  - exactly one line `[WARN] MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE: task task-postflight -- the merged tree <M> on <B> was not frozen, recorded and passed by the check VMs (<CODE>[ environment=<ENV>]); main did not move and the task's bytes stay on moe/task/task-postflight.`
  Both lines are full-line matches.

REFUSED ROWS. All run with FAKE_ATTEMPT_PROFILE=verified-local: one per DoD 2 case, plus the comment-732e84b5 pair.
- SG-nonzero: not-passed -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_NOT_PASSED. This is the end-state pin the planner asked for. On the code-failure observation, the daemon's repair moves REVIEW to WORKING (repairActivation.ts applyRepairDecision; updateTask clears the assignee) before this finalize. routeUnlandedLanding then keeps a non-REVIEW row's status and assignment while it records landingRetry (workerLifecycle.ts). So the real end state is WORKING, unassigned, landingRetry {gate, 1}, attempt closed. This row pins the wrapper's half: one unlanded 'gate' finalize, the attempt closed, the stored retry, and no status write of its own.
- SG-stopped: stopped with FAKE_CHECK_DISPATCH_CODE=RUNNER_VM_DELETE_FAILED -> RUNNER_VM_DELETE_FAILED.
- SG-nothing-owed: stopped RUNNER_NOTHING_OWED.
- SG-undeclared: stopped RUNNER_DEPENDENCIES_UNDECLARED.
- SG-missing: MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH=$TMP_DIR/no-such-dispatch.js -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_UNAVAILABLE, with no check-dispatch row.
- SG-crash: crash -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_NO_REPORT.
- SG-unparsable: garbage (exit 0) -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_REPLY_INVALID.
- SG-env: stopped RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT_NOT_APPROVED with FAKE_CHECK_DISPATCH_ENVIRONMENT=moe-local-vm-v1:<a 64-char lowercase hex literal> -> the REFUSED line ends with environment=<that id>.
- SG-env-malformed: the same with 64 UPPERCASE hex -> the code alone.
- SG-timeout: hang with MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SEC=2 -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT. A check-dispatch-term row shows TERM reached the job's group, and the run takes under 60 s (SECONDS).

SG-PROTECTED. Copy the VR-protected invocation (VMR_CMD=claude, a not-ready verified-local readiness, MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1, MOE_DAEMON_PATH=$TMP_DIR/fake-daemon.js) and add MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH=$SG_FAKE. Expect exit 1, exactly one MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH_IGNORED line, and the override path never printed.

End with `echo "[strong gate] ok SG-pass, legacy, observe, nonzero, stopped, nothing-owed, undeclared, missing, crash, unparsable, env, env-malformed, timeout, protected"`.

Error handling in the harness: each row fails through vmr_fail with the row name and OUT. A missing or extra row, line or RPC fails it; nothing skips.

postflight-vm-route.sh [strong gate]: the sliced rows, in the same section. Slice the functions with vmc_slice (a top-level helper) and run them under set -e, as the [strong intent] GSI driver does.

(a) SGV, the verdict table. A driver of `check_dispatch_verdict` alone, run as `env PYTHON_CMD="$PY" bash <driver> <file> <rc>` with TASK=task-v and CANDIDATE=cand-v. Each row writes the reply bytes with printf and compares stdout exactly. The rows:
- empty, at rc 0 and at rc 3 -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_NO_REPORT;
- `not json` -> REPLY_INVALID; `[1]` -> REPLY_INVALID;
- a pass object (task-v, cand-v, one passed result) at rc 0 -> PASS; the same without its trailing newline -> PASS; the same at rc 2 -> MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_NOT_PASSED;
- candidateId cand-other -> REPLY_INVALID; taskId task-other -> REPLY_INVALID; results [] at rc 0 -> REPLY_INVALID;
- a log line before the pass line -> REPLY_INVALID;
- {stopped:{code:'RUNNER_NOTHING_OWED'}} at rc 0 -> RUNNER_NOTHING_OWED (a stop beats exit 0);
- {stopped:{code:'lower case'}} -> REPLY_INVALID;
- {code:'RUNNER_SEAM_UNAVAILABLE'} -> RUNNER_SEAM_UNAVAILABLE; {code:'bad code'} -> REPLY_INVALID;
- a stop plus a top-level code -> the stopped code;
- stopped RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT_NOT_APPROVED with a valid id -> `RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT_NOT_APPROVED environment=<id>`;
- the same stop with each malformed id -> the code alone. The malformed ids: text before the prefix; the valid id plus a trailing newline inside the JSON string; uppercase hex; 63 hex; a number; null. Per mem:decision-verified-local-check-gate item 5, a dropped anchor survived mutation there until a leading-text row existed;
- a reply over 1 MiB -> REPLY_INVALID.

(b) SGU, the runner. A driver of resolve_check_dispatch_cli, run_check_dispatch, stop_check_dispatch, check_dispatch_verdict, heartbeat_sidecar_running and land_lease_budget. It sets `CHECK_DISPATCH_GRACE_SEC="${SGU_GRACE:-120}"`, then runs `resolve_check_dispatch_cli; rc=0; run_check_dispatch || rc=$?; echo "rc=$rc code=$CHECK_DISPATCH_CODE"`.

The fixture:
- a scratch repo $SGU/project with one commit, used as FROZEN_COMMIT;
- a candidate file .moe/candidates/cand-sgu.json {id:'cand-sgu', taskId:'task-sgu', treeSha, createdAt};
- SECURE_TEMP_DIR=$SGU/sec;
- SCRIPT_DIR=$SGU/scripts, whose local-runner/check-dispatch.mjs is a two-line ESM stub: `import { createRequire } from 'node:module';` then `createRequire(import.meta.url)(process.env.SGU_FAKE);`. The bundled path then runs the same fake, and its row's entry names the stub;
- the five credentials exported.

The rows:
- U1: no override, mode code with RUNNER_SEAM_UNAVAILABLE -> `rc=1 code=RUNNER_SEAM_UNAVAILABLE`, entry = the stub, no IGNORED line.
- U2: MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH=$SG_FAKE with RUNTIME_PROTECTED=0, pass -> `rc=0 code=`, entry = $SG_FAKE, exact argv, credentials [] and the [OK] line.
- U3: the same override with RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1 -> the stub ran (entry), exactly one MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH_IGNORED line, and the override path is never printed (DoD 4).
- U4: MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SEC set to each of 0, -1, abc, 86401 and 1.0001 -> `rc=1 code=MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_INVALID`, with no check-dispatch row.
- U5: hang-hard with MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SEC=1 and SGU_GRACE=1 -> `rc=1 code=MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT` within 15 s; `kill -0 <the fake's recorded pid>` then fails. That is a probe only; it proves the KILL fallback reached the TERM-ignoring child.
- U6: MOE_REL=sub -> `rc=1 code=MOE_WORKTREE_PROJECT_NOT_TOP` with its line, and no check-dispatch row.

(c) SG8, a static check that reuses G8's BODY and gline:
- the body has exactly one line containing run_check_dispatch and exactly one containing strong_landing_task;
- the strong condition line is exactly `        if [ -n "${QUALITY_GATE:-}" ] && [ -n "${LAND_TASK_ID:-}" ] && strong_landing_task "$LAND_TASK_ID"; then`;
- the legacy line is exactly `        elif [ -n "${QUALITY_GATE:-}" ] && ! { freeze_candidate "$b" "$m" && run_frozen_gate worktree; }; then`;
- the order is: the strong condition, then run_check_dispatch, then the legacy elif, then the wt_strong_intent line.

End the section with `echo "[strong gate] ok SGV, SGU U1-U6 and SG8"`.

Error handling: every mismatch fails through vmc_fail, naming the row and the got and expected text.
